257
00:15:33,500 --> 00:15:34,330
No kidding.

258
00:15:34,413 --> 00:15:35,860
Changing shape, closing in.

259
00:15:37,320 --> 00:15:40,680
I'm warning you now, don't
try anything. Death 13?

260
00:15:44,240 --> 00:15:48,711
Kakyoin, you have to get Hierophant
away from his back before it's too late.

261
00:15:49,800 --> 00:15:50,630
Pouted.

262
00:15:51,900 --> 00:15:53,520
I'll chop you in half!

263
00:15:57,080 --> 00:15:57,910
Impossible.

264
00:15:59,440 --> 00:16:00,860
How could he do that?

265
00:16:01,780 --> 00:16:02,610
He...

266
00:16:02,693 --> 00:16:04,440
he chopped himself in half!

267
00:16:07,820 --> 00:16:09,320
Kick! No!

268
00:16:11,040 --> 00:16:12,040
Lally-ho!

269
00:16:12,720 --> 00:16:14,417
Haven't you figured it out yet?

270
00:16:14,500 --> 00:16:18,029
Death-13's body is as hollow
as the space between your ears!

271
00:16:19,280 --> 00:16:24,400
My stand is only comprised of the head,
arms, and the giant siphon wheels!

272
00:16:24,620 --> 00:16:26,540
You gigantic ignoramuses!

273
00:16:28,060 --> 00:16:28,890
Let's see.

274
00:16:29,140 --> 00:16:30,905
Given the way the stands work,

275
00:16:31,160 --> 00:16:35,097
Kakyoin's body should also be split
in two inside the sleeping bag.

276
00:16:35,180 --> 00:16:36,500
Nah, just kidding.

277
00:16:37,240 --> 00:16:38,070
Kakyoin!

278
00:16:38,153 --> 00:16:39,944
Hey, you sure you're all right?

279
00:16:40,660 --> 00:16:42,200
Please take a closer look.

280
00:16:42,420 --> 00:16:44,917
Surely you know Hierophant
isn't that careless.

281
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:49,118
He wouldn't just stay on the enemy's
back without a plan in the wings.

282
00:16:55,820 --> 00:16:57,460
He's not chopped in half,

283
00:16:57,660 --> 00:17:02,080
he's turned into a snake-like thing
and he's slithering into my ear!

284
00:17:14,540 --> 00:17:16,680
My arm is moving on its own!

285
00:17:18,620 --> 00:17:20,380
No, it's coming in!

286
00:17:25,520 --> 00:17:27,260
I told you before,

287
00:17:27,520 --> 00:17:31,357
my stand was in your blind spot,
and your scythe couldn't cut him.

288
00:17:31,440 --> 00:17:33,969
Now then, unless you'd
like to be destroyed

289
00:17:34,180 --> 00:17:35,137
from the inside out?

290
00:17:35,220 --> 00:17:36,397
How about you do me a favor?

291
00:17:36,480 --> 00:17:38,127
and heal the cuts on my arm?

292
00:17:38,520 --> 00:17:40,814
Anything is possible in a dream, right?

293
00:17:40,940 --> 00:17:42,860
So healing a cut should be easy.

294
00:17:43,900 --> 00:17:44,730
Right!

295
00:17:56,000 --> 00:17:58,280
All right, everyone, time to wake up.

296
00:18:01,740 --> 00:18:03,920
Come on, Polnareff, up and at him.

297
00:18:04,120 --> 00:18:06,532
There's a nice breakfast waiting for you.

298
00:18:10,340 --> 00:18:13,046
I feel like I had a
terrible dream last night.

299
00:18:13,180 --> 00:18:14,010
You and me both.

300
00:18:14,093 --> 00:18:18,800
I can't remember it, but I have the
sneaking suspicion that it was terrifying.

301
00:18:21,540 --> 00:18:22,370
Kakuine!

302
00:18:22,800 --> 00:18:23,840
Are you okay?

303
00:18:24,120 --> 00:18:26,317
How are you like a deranged
lunatic last night?

304
00:18:26,400 --> 00:18:28,518
You even carved letters in your arm.

305
00:18:29,940 --> 00:18:30,770
Wait.

306
00:18:30,853 --> 00:18:33,497
What where did the wound go?

307
00:18:33,580 --> 00:18:35,017
All right.

308
00:18:35,100 --> 00:18:37,571
I think I'll change the baby's diaper now.

309
00:18:38,720 --> 00:18:40,017
What in the world?

310
00:18:40,100 --> 00:18:43,177
It's morning, sleepyhead.

311
00:18:43,260 --> 00:18:46,077
He seems to be getting along
famously with the baby.

312
00:18:46,160 --> 00:18:48,157
Maybe I just dreamed the whole thing.

313
00:18:48,240 --> 00:18:51,497
Well, then did you have a good rest?

314
00:18:51,580 --> 00:18:53,800
Oh well, never mind.

315
00:19:01,280 --> 00:19:02,515
Everyone's forgotten.

316
00:19:02,880 --> 00:19:06,160
A stand whose very existence
is completely forgotten.

317
00:19:06,880 --> 00:19:08,720
What a strange creature.

318
00:19:09,560 --> 00:19:11,840
But I haven't forgotten anything.

319
00:19:12,260 --> 00:19:16,495
Since I brought my stand into the
dream with me, my memories are intact.

320
00:19:17,800 --> 00:19:18,630
Injure you.

321
00:19:18,940 --> 00:19:21,020
We'll take you to a nearby town.

322
00:19:21,360 --> 00:19:23,654
You need to be returned to your mother.

323
00:19:24,140 --> 00:19:26,860
However, don't come
anywhere near us again.

324
00:19:27,260 --> 00:19:29,495
If you do, you'll have to be punished.

325
00:19:32,260 --> 00:19:34,180
in a manner such as this.

326
00:19:35,360 --> 00:19:36,190
Huh?

327
00:19:36,273 --> 00:19:37,460
Is that my poop?

328
00:19:44,180 --> 00:19:48,680
Oh, Cocule, I see you've made
some baby food for the little lad.

329
00:19:49,520 --> 00:19:50,900
Yes, good work.

330
00:19:51,180 --> 00:19:53,298
I'm sure he must be starving by now.

331
00:19:55,400 --> 00:19:57,460
Hey, no, you wouldn't!

332
00:20:00,340 --> 00:20:01,300
Eat up!

333
00:20:01,580 --> 00:20:03,286
These yum-yums are delicious!

334
00:20:04,100 --> 00:20:05,220
Say-ya!

335
00:20:09,480 --> 00:20:10,420
This again?

336
00:20:10,720 --> 00:20:11,838
What's the problem?

337
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:14,235
It's as if he doesn't like this stuff.

338
00:20:14,360 --> 00:20:16,831
At this rate, I'll have to force-feed him.

339
00:20:17,120 --> 00:20:17,950
Stop!

340
00:20:19,140 --> 00:20:21,040
You can't force it, Mr. Joestar.

341
00:20:21,320 --> 00:20:24,202
If you do, he'll just end
up hating it even more.

342
00:20:24,300 --> 00:20:26,340
In special cases like this.

343
00:20:39,300 --> 00:20:41,457
I told you it was delicious.

344
00:20:41,540 --> 00:20:44,520
It is, ba-dum-bum.

345
00:20:53,500 --> 00:20:56,417
Joestar and the others have now
crossed the Arabian Peninsula

346
00:20:56,500 --> 00:20:59,177
and are currently making
their way across the Red Sea?

347
00:20:59,260 --> 00:21:01,880
as they prepare to enter Egypt. But!

348
00:21:03,760 --> 00:21:06,360
Hey, old man, something's off.

349
00:21:06,840 --> 00:21:08,781
You're going the wrong direction.

350
00:21:09,220 --> 00:21:13,680
If you're headed to Egypt, shouldn't
you be traveling directly west? Hmm?

351
00:21:15,060 --> 00:21:17,531
You seem to be heading toward that island.

352
00:21:18,120 --> 00:21:19,880
That's right. Nice deduction.

353
00:21:20,300 --> 00:21:22,957
I've had my reasons for
keeping this to myself.

354
00:21:23,040 --> 00:21:26,617
But before we arrive in Egypt,
we need to make a slight detour.

355
00:21:26,700 --> 00:21:29,053
Someone is waiting for us on the island.

356
00:21:29,460 --> 00:21:30,290
Hmm.

357
00:21:30,720 --> 00:21:33,838
He's a man who is extremely
important to our journey.

358
00:21:34,940 --> 00:21:36,705
What is that supposed to mean?

359
00:21:56,580 --> 00:21:59,277
All the old paintings on the tomb.

360
00:21:59,360 --> 00:22:01,317
They do the sand dance, don't you know?

361
00:22:01,400 --> 00:22:03,557
If you move too quick, go away.

362
00:22:03,640 --> 00:22:05,977
They're falling down like a domino.

363
00:22:06,060 --> 00:22:08,637
On the buzzer man by the Nile.

364
00:22:08,720 --> 00:22:10,677
He got the money on a bet.

365
00:22:10,760 --> 00:22:12,297
Called crocodiles.

366
00:22:12,380 --> 00:22:13,210
Oh-eh-oh.

367
00:22:13,293 --> 00:22:15,237
But I snap their teeth on your cigarette.

368
00:22:15,320 --> 00:22:17,477
Fall in touch with a hookah. I say.

369
00:22:17,560 --> 00:22:19,757
Oh-eh-oh.

370
00:22:19,840 --> 00:22:24,777
Oh-eh-oh.

371
00:22:24,860 --> 00:22:26,500
Walk like an Egyptian.

372
00:22:37,200 --> 00:22:40,177
The blonde waitresses take their trays.

373
00:22:40,260 --> 00:22:42,177
Spin around and they cross the floor.

374
00:22:42,260 --> 00:22:43,697
They've got the moves.

375
00:22:43,780 --> 00:22:46,437
You drop your drink. All the school kids.

376
00:22:46,520 --> 00:22:47,937
So sick of folks.

377
00:22:48,020 --> 00:22:49,997
They're like the punk and the metal band.

378
00:22:50,080 --> 00:22:51,560
When the buzzer rings.

379
00:22:52,280 --> 00:22:54,237
They're walking like an Egyptian.

380
00:22:54,320 --> 00:22:56,917
All the kids in the marketplace say.

381
00:22:57,000 --> 00:22:57,877
Walk

382
00:22:57,960 --> 00:23:04,960
like

383
00:23:05,060 --> 00:23:05,890
an Egyptian.

384
00:23:09,220 --> 00:23:13,597
I ended up killing my friend,
there's nothing I could possibly do.

385
00:23:13,680 --> 00:23:16,757
Allow me to thank you for
freeing me from the lab.

386
00:23:16,840 --> 00:23:18,917
I wouldn't believe it
if it wasn't right here.

387
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:20,457
Tell me your three wishes.

388
00:23:20,540 --> 00:23:23,360
Do you have the ability to revive someone?
